-- title:
--   Supersingular affine chart over the level field at q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 2$ (the hypothesis `hq2`), $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and a guard prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$ is fixed. Here `fieldBar q M'` denotes the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (inside Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) of the function field of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ attached to the subgroup `levelH q M'` of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$, namely the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; and `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, the field generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the series $q$-expansions $j(q^{d})$ for the divisors $d \mid M'$.
--
--   The following data are assumed.
--
--   *Valuation ring and supersingular places.* $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$, in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`LiesOverPrime`); $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, i.e. those places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places for level $M'$, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(j) \in$ `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`; $s$ is an element of $W$. There is an inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` into `fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   *Constant reduction.* $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` along $A$ onto `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` contracting to $A$ along the structure map, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the level-$M'$ function field over the residue field of $A$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal of `R₀.integers`, compatible with the residue map of $A$ on constants, together with a map on places preserving degrees and matching push-forward of principal divisors with orders of residues, and the property that every nonzero element can be scaled by a constant into the integers with nonzero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   *Small constants.* $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lies in $A$; the contraction $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; and `hκ` states that every $a \in A$ differs from some $c \in k_0 \cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   *Auxiliary prime and roots of unity.* $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   *Base layer.* $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $K_b = \bot$, $A_b$ is a valuation subring of $K_b$ whose elements are exactly those whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $A$, and $\varpi_b \neq 0$ generates the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   The conclusion is stated for `fieldBar q M'` regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`. Let $F_0$ be any intermediate field of $k_0 \subseteq$ `fieldBar q M'` which consists exactly of those $f$ all of whose Laurent coefficients $f_n$, $n \in \mathbb Z$, lie in $k_0$. Then there exists a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with the following nine properties.
--
--   (i) For $x \in k_0$: $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (ii) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (iii) The image of $\pi_0$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (iv) (Specialisation to $s$.) For every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb Q$ belonging to `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `R₀.integers`, if $g$ is regular wherever $j$ is, in the sense that every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(j_q)$ satisfies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(g)$, and if the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, then the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` under `hle` lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; moreover, for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in the residue field of $A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference between that image and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (v) (Level stability of $W_0$.) For every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (the primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every $f \in F_0$ such that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` also lies in $F_0$: $f \in W_0$ if and only if `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in W_0$.
--
--   (vi)–(ix) (Affine chart.) There exist a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that:
--
--   — the structure map $A_b \to B$ is the inclusion $A_b \subseteq K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`;
--
--   — $B$ is contained in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subextension generated by the image of $K_b$, and conversely every element of that compositum is of the form $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$, $h \neq 0$;
--
--   — $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$, and $B/(\varpi_b B)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$;
--
--   — every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is a prime element; and $W_0$ is the corresponding localisation: $f \in F_0$ lies in $W_0$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and the image of $\varpi_b$ not dividing $h$;
--
--   — the image of $j_q$ in `fieldBar q M'` under `hle` lies in $B$, and $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$;
--
--   — (identification of the special fibre with a Drinfeld quotient curve) for every algebra structure of the field $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ = `GaloisField q 2` on the residue field $\kappa$ of $A$, every witness that the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to the fixed field [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the subfield of the Drinfeld function field fixed by the action of $C_s$) such that: the cardinality of $C_s$ equals `placeWidthChar q M' s`, which for $q = 2$ is $12$ divided by the ramification index `placeRamificationJ M' s` when $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(j) = 0$ and $1/\text{that index}$ otherwise; the kernel of $\rho$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ composed with $A_b \to B$ is reduction $A_b \to \kappa$ followed by the structure map of the quotient field; every element of the quotient field is of the form $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $g,h \in B$; an element $z$ of the quotient field lies in the range of $\rho$ precisely when its image in the Drinfeld function field lies in the image of [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21); and $\rho$ is equivariant: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ such that the pair $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ lies in the subgroup [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), and every $f \in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹ f` $\in B$, the image under $\rho$ of the latter, read in the Drinfeld function field, equals the action of that pair through [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) on $\rho(f)$.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ case, under the rigidifying hypothesis that a prime $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ divides $M'$, of the construction of the local ring at a supersingular place together with an affine chart of the supersingular component of the special fibre of the full-level modular curve at $q$, over the level field $F_0$ of elements whose $q$-expansion coefficients lie in $k_0$; the chart is identified modulo $\varpi_b$ with a quotient of a Drinfeld curve over the residue field, compatibly with the $\Gamma_0(M')$-level action. It is obtained from the companion statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_nodes_of_levelField_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_nodes_of_levelField_of_eq_two_of_dvd), which also records the nodes of the chart, and is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_affineChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_affineChart_of_eq_two_of_dvd).
